Two important points:

1. For all practical purposes, you can only write scrolls you have
   already identified.

2. Don't write most scrolls you might want until you have blessed your
   magic marker, or you have a blessed scroll.

Assuming you have identified the following scrolls, I might write:

   blessed scroll of charging: high priority, to recharge marker

   blessed scrolls of enchant weapon: +8 darts are pretty handy, and you
                                      need some decent weapon

   scroll of teleportation: if you want to rob a shop (like the used
			    armor store you found earlier) or as a last
			    resort when you are in trouble

   blessed scroll of remove curse: if you come across a ghost level

   blessed scroll of genocide: weapon of mass destruction
   uncursed scroll of genocide: rust monsters
   cursed scroll of genocide: nurses = lots of hitpoints (not that vital
                              in your case, having 18 constitution)

   blessed scroll of enchant armor: not really necessary at the moment 
				    but useful later

   blessed scroll of identify: also not really necessary at the moment 

   scroll of destroy armor: to get rid of any nasty cursed armor (if you
                            are desperate, like -3 gauntlets of fumbling)
                            
Since there are a lot of possibilities, I wouldn't write anything in
your situation until I had blessed the magic marker. then I would write
a scroll of charging and two of enchant weapon, and leave the rest for
later.

B.T.W, the above are not the exact spellings. When prompted, just type
the actual name, ie; "enchant weapon", not "blessed scroll of enchant
weapon". The relative state of marker and scroll determines the
blessed/cursed status.

